# CLAUDE.md

<!--
  This is a TEMPLATE. Copy it to your repo root as `CLAUDE.md`, delete the
  parts you do not need, and replace every PLACEHOLDER path/value below.

  What this file is for:
  Adopting the `sutra` profile in-repo so that teammates who have NOT
  installed the sutra plugin still pick up its guidance automatically when
  they open this project in Claude Code.

  You usually do NOT need this file.
  If the sutra plugin is installed in a teammate's Claude Code, the profile
  is already active for them globally -- no CLAUDE.md change is required.
  Use the in-repo approach below only when you want the profile to travel
  WITH the repository (e.g. for contributors who have not installed the
  plugin, or for CI/agent runs that start from a clean checkout).
-->

<!--
  OPTION A -- @import a vendored/submoduled profile.

  Vendor the sutra repo into your project (git submodule, subtree, or a
  plain clone under a `vendor/` directory), then import the profile file
  you want. The line below pulls the "standard" profile; swap the filename
  for another profile (for example `strict.md`) to change the ruleset.

  IMPORTANT: @import resolves LOCAL PATHS ONLY. It cannot fetch a URL or a
  remote git ref. The path must exist on disk relative to this file at the
  time Claude Code reads it. Keep the vendored copy checked in (or wired up
  as a submodule your teammates initialize) so the path always resolves.

  Replace the PLACEHOLDER path with wherever you vendored sutra.
-->
@vendor/sutra/plugins/sutra/profiles/standard.md

<!--
  OPTION B -- pick the profile with a `.sutra` marker file (plugin users).

  If teammates DO have the sutra plugin installed, you can skip the @import
  entirely. Instead, drop a file named `.sutra` at the repo root whose only
  contents are the profile name, for example:

      strict

  The plugin reads that marker and applies the named profile to this repo.
  This is the lightest-touch option, but it only affects people who already
  have the plugin -- it does nothing for a clean checkout without the plugin.

  Rule of thumb:
    - Want the profile to work for everyone, plugin or not -> Option A.
    - Everyone on the team has the plugin -> Option B (a one-line `.sutra`).
  Do not use both at once; pick one so there is a single source of truth.
-->

